<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48462" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tmōlus</span></b>  and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tĭmōlus</span></b> , i,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τμῶλος,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a mountain of Lydia
				in which the Pactolus rises</i>, <i>producing
				excellent wines</i>, now <i>Kisilja Mousa
			Dagh</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 29, 30, § 110</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. G. 1,
				56</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 2, 217</span></i>; <i><span class="en">11, 151</span></i>
			sq.— 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Form Timolus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					6, 15</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">11, 86</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A town near Mount Tmolus</i>, <i><span class="en">Tac. A. 2,
			47</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A small river flowing from Mount Tmolus</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 33,
				8, 43, § 126</span></i>. — Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tmōlĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to Tmolus</i>, <i>Tmolian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					P. 4, 15, 9</span></i>
			.— <i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tmōlĭus</span></b> ,
			ii, m. (sc. mons), <i>Mount
				Tmolus</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. G. 2,
			98</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tmō-lītes</span></b> ,
				is, <i>adj. m.</i>, <i>of Tmolus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vicanus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Fl. 3, 8</span></i>
			.—Subst., <i>the wine of
				Tmolus</i>, <i>Tmolian wine</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 14, 7,
				9, § 74</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vitr. 7, 3</span></i>.</div>
